  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DDF- &apos;Space 4 Women Empwment&amp;Inclusion&apos;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dew Drop Foundation (DDF) is one of the former empowerment grantees of Voice in Nigeria. Their former project worked on transformational change for women &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; young people, in Umuode Community, under which women secured spaces within the community leadership system and this milestone was adopted in the revised constitution of the community. Current project is interested in strengthening the capacity of these women to be financially independence and politically ready, to leverage opportunities within the political spaces &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; community structures, for more inclusive &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; progressive Umuode community.

Current project titled &#x2018;Our Space for Empowerment and Inclusion&#x2019; seeks to strengthen the economic capacity, voice, and participation of women in governance in Umuode Community, Nkanu East LGA, Enugu State.  The project will consolidate and scale up the gains of previous project by building the capacities of more women in leadership and strategic advocacy aimed at promoting women&#x2019;s access to resources, (particularlyland) for cooperative farming and sustainable income generation. This would reduce their economic vulnerability, enhance their self-reliance, amplify their voices in the community and protect them from sexual exploitation and violence.

Key activities intended to drive these outcomesinclude
i. Capacity building/training workshops on leadership and advocacy to enable the women leaders utilize their space in the Traditional Ruler/Igwe&apos;s Council effectively to speak for themselves. Likewise, more women with leadership potentials would be identified and trained to support advocacy activities.
ii. Voice Roundtable for monthly dialogues led by the women who are members of the Traditional Council with support from DDF to share ideas, address challenges, strategize and coordinate advocacy activities to advance women rights and access to resources in Umuode.
iii. Facilitate the acquisition and access to land resources for cooperative farming and sustainable income generation for women.
iv. Enterprise Development Clinics to host trainings and mentorship for women on local product processing and innovation, marketing strategy, branding, sales, finance, access to credit and market.

DDF hopes that this project will help to bridge the gap of socio-political inequality perpetuated by the patriarchal system in Igbo Land, where Umuode community belongs. They believe that Umuode&#x2019;s case will be an example for other communities to rise up and challenge these anomalies-  &#x2018;every little effort matter&#x2019;.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dewdrop Foundation (DDF) is a not-for-profit organization that is focused on improving the livelihoods of vulnerable groups in the society, especially in rural communities, by developing their capacity to fight for their rights; and engage in enterprisesthat guarantee them sustainable livelihoods.

DDF started as an organization whose work largely focused on Caregivers. However, our field experience over the years on the intersecting challenges faced by rights holders, led to our additional focus on community development issues as key for addressing and eliminating the root causes of labor and human rights abuses in rural communities.

Their mission is to build the capacity of communities especially the vulnerable populations to become self-reliant and empowered through inclusive governance and sustainable development interventions. Their vision is for a Inclusive communities where everyone, even the most vulnerable people are empowered, protected, and thrive sustainably.

These are their non-negotiables and the spirit behind their vision.
1. Integrity
2. Transparency
3.  Inclusivity
4. Problem solving
5. Professionalism

Their strategic focus are as follows:

&#x2022; To protect and advance the rights of women and vulnerable groups
&#x2022; To empowervulnerable populations through specialized care giving and livelihood skills development for self-reliance
&#x2022; To strengthen the capacity of communities to facilitate sustainable development by addressing intersectional issues through the GHEEES model focusing on Governance, Health, Education, Enterprise, Environment and Security to drive community growth and advancement

DDF is duly registered with appropriate government authorities such as CAC &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; SCUML etc.</narrative>
